---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";
import { route } from "../lib/catalogue";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "anatomy", label: "Anatomy", heading: false },
  { id: "timing", label: "When it shows and hides" },
  { id: "touch", label: "Touch and clicks" },
  { id: "accessibility", label: "Accessibility" },
  { id: "methods", label: "Options and methods" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="hover_card" sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.anatomy}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          A hover card previews where a link goes, such as a person or an article, when
          the link is hovered or gets keyboard focus.
        </p>
        <p>
          Add <code>hover-card-trigger</code> to an <code>&lt;a href&gt;</code> and point
          its <code>aria-details</code> at the card, a <a href={route('popover')}>popover</a>
          with <code>popover="hint"</code>. <code>AutoInit()</code> starts every
          <code>.hover-card-trigger</code>. The card looks like a popover and sits below
          the link with their start edges aligned, flipped to the other side when it
          would not fit.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Written by <a class="hover-card-trigger" href="#ada" aria-details="demo-ada-card">Ada Lovelace</a>.
        </p>
        <div id="demo-ada-card" class="popover" popover="hint">
          <h3>Ada Lovelace</h3>
          <p>Mathematician. Wrote the first published program, for the Analytical Engine.</p>
          <p><a href="#ada">All articles by Ada</a></p>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<p>Written by <a class="hover-card-trigger" href="/people/ada"
                 aria-details="ada-card">Ada Lovelace</a>.</p>
<div id="ada-card" class="popover" popover="hint">
  <h3>Ada Lovelace</h3>
  <p>Mathematician. Wrote the first published program, for the Analytical Engine.</p>
  <p><a href="/people/ada/articles">All articles by Ada</a></p>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.timing}>
        <p>
          The card shows once the pointer or keyboard focus has rested on the link for
          <code>enterDelay</code>, 500&nbsp;ms by default, so a pointer that only passes
          over the link shows nothing. It stays while the pointer is on the link or the
          card, and while focus is on either. When both are left, it hides after
          <code>exitDelay</code>, 300&nbsp;ms by default, which is time enough for a
          pointer to cross the gap to the card.
        </p>
        <p>
          Focus stays on the link when the card shows, and Tab moves into the card's
          links and buttons. Escape hides the card and takes focus in it back to the
          link. A click elsewhere hides it too. One hint card shows at a time, and a hover
          card leaves an open <a href={route('menu')}>menu</a> or popover alone.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.touch}>
        <p>
          A tap or click follows the link and shows no card, so the linked page has to
          hold the same content for touch screens. Keep the card a short preview, and put
          anything to act on in the page, a popover opened by a button or a
          <a href={route('dialogs')}>dialog</a>. Do not also give the link
          <code>interestfor</code>, which Chromium would handle on its own as well.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.accessibility}>
        <p>
          <code>aria-details</code> tells a screen reader that the link has more detail
          and lets it move there. Screen readers support it unevenly, and a hidden card is
          not in the reading order at all, which is another reason the linked page must
          hold the same content. Leave the role off the card: it can hold links, which a
          <a href={route('tooltips')}>tooltip</a> cannot.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.methods}>
        <p>
          <code>enterDelay</code> and <code>exitDelay</code> take milliseconds, from script
          or from <code>data-hover-card-options</code>. The link fires
          <code>expressive:open</code> and <code>expressive:close</code> when the card shows
          and hides, also when the browser hides it.
        </p>
<Code code={`
<a class="hover-card-trigger" href="/people/ada" aria-details="ada-card"
   data-hover-card-options='{"enterDelay":300,"exitDelay":200}'>Ada Lovelace</a>
<div id="ada-card" class="popover" popover="hint">…</div>
`} />
<Code code={`
const card = Expressive.HoverCard.getInstance(document.querySelector('.hover-card-trigger'));
card.open();    // shows the card now, without enterDelay
card.close();   // hides it now, without exitDelay
card.destroy(); // hides a card it showed and removes the listeners
`} />
  </Section>
</DocsLayout>
